em if you obey the Messenger, it means to obey Allah, so it means the Quran So then Allah saying obey Allah is enough, he doesn't need to say obey the Messenger But in reality, all of these verses are like a thorn in their throats They know that these are two different types of obediences, that's why Allahﷻ mentions two types of obediences He doesn't just say obey Allah and His Messenger, but He says obey Allah \"and obey\"..", "So, He adds the word \"obey\" specifically for the Messenger to show that these are two different types of obediences, Which shows the importance of listening and obeying to the Messengerﷺ in that which he will be teaching, And where is that thing that the Prophetﷺ is teaching? Because the Prophet is sent to everyone, he's not just sent to his Companions So me and you and all the believers need to find that thing; and that is as we say is of course the Hadith",))
