at will mean it is not preserved literally, because there's many people who read it and think it's the Quran So if you say مَلِكِ is the only right way or مَٰلِكِ is the only right way; then you've admitted that the Quran has been changed Because the other word is not going to be the words of Allah, it's going to be the words of human beings,", "And if you say that both of them are correct, Then show us where does the Quran say that the Quran has been revealed in many different ways? Reading the Quran can be in many different ways.. Where is that in the Quran? Where does the Quran mention that Allah revealed the Quran in different dialects and different ways of recitation? You need to show us where does the Quran say that explicitly, not your own twist and games Where does the Quran explicitly say that it's been revealed in different ways, For you to recite it in different ways with different dialects?", "So if you cannot find us that in the Quran, then you have to accept that by no doubt it is in the Hadith And the Hadith is the evidence and the Hadith is Revelation from Allahﷻ, and it explains this idea; This phenomena that Muslims have accepted for 1400 years, that there is Revelation other than the Quran And that Allahﷻ revealed the Quran in different dialects and different أحرف OK, so now moving on to the second part of the video, which is the criticism and logical inconsistencies of those Hadith rejectors And how their methods are completely inconsistent and illogical, and I will give a very easy example..", "The Hadith rejecters say that we reject Hadith, because men are fallible and they can make mistakes And we don't trust that they completely transmitted this information correctly We will ask them this simple question: Who transmitted to you the Quran? If you claim that the Hadith is corrupted because men are fallible and they make mistakes, We will say also you have to use the same argument for the Quran! Because the people who gave you the Hadith are the