 now people who are strong memorisers, who narrated from the same individual, And now we can know this is a mistake by the Narrator So that is something we call شُذوذ (irregularity) And then you have عِلّة (which is a hidden defect), The source of the Narration– a person could be narrating from the Traditions of Jews and Christians, for instance,", "And he mistakenly would attribute it to the Prophet And then that would be a hidden defect So he didn't mean to attribute to the Prophet, but he forgot, so he mistakenly attributed to the Prophet So there's a hidden defect in the Narration Then we know: now actually the source of this Narration is إسرائليات (israelite narrations) It's not from the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, And this is an example, right? There's many other hidden defects that exist There's many other irregularities I'm just trying to simplify this as much as possible It's a heavy science, but yeah, hopefully that makes sense",))
