#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("I'll give two very basic examples: There's a great scholar who's called Yahya Ibn Ma'een Yahya Ibn Ma'een is a great scholar who used to handle the grading of Ahadith and seeing who is reliable and who's not One day –they have something called TESTING the person who narrates the Hadith– As we said, the person who narrates Hadith has to have a strong memory, So what they do is that they used to TEST the reliability of the memory of these individuals, –the people that are known to be trustworthy that narrate Narrations of the Prophetﷺ–, they used to go and test them Yahya Ibn Ma'een went one time to one of his teachers, Alfadl Ibn Dukayn, who is a major scholar, well known of strong memory But even though he was well known of strong memory, and in the community they know that this person has a strong memory,", "They said still, we have to actually investigate, we have to actually see whether he has a strong memory or not, let’s actually test him So what Yahya Ibn Ma'een did, is that he went to him and then he mixed some of his Narrations with another person's Narrations In order for him to test Alfadl Ibn Dukayn whether, he actually has a strong memory or not So that was a regular thing the scholars used to do at the time, they used to go to different Narrators and they used to test them And you do not know when they're going to test you, who is going to test you So, if you have a weak memory, then they will label you after testing you that you have a weak memory, And then people -whoever narrates from you- that Narration would be not reliable, Will be doubted because the memory of that individual is not strong", "Also for example Yahya Ibn Ma'een –they were very specific–, he used to sit in a sitting, and a person narrates Hadith, And then there are students who are taking the Hadith and writing it down.. So, Yahya Ibn Ma'een noticed one individual who slept. So then YIM wrote down at which number of the Hadith did he sleep He slept when the 4th Hadith was being narrated, And then when he woke up again, Yahya Ibn Ma'een wrote down that he woke up at the 11th Hadith So they were so strict to make sure what he directly heard and what he did not hear If that individual leaves the sitting of knowledge and goes and narrates a Hadith, they will say to him: \"Where did you hear this Hadith from?", "You were sleeping\" \"We know that you didn't hear this Hadith from that sitting, so where did you get this information from?\" They were so strict to the extent of making sure that the individuals, even though they're sitting down In the same sitting of knowledge, that they're writing down what exactly they heard 100% And we can even see this idea of reliability, it was from the beginning From the time of the first Caliphate of Islam, right directly after the death of the Prophetﷺ The first Caliphate of Islam who ruled only for like 3 years after the Prophetﷺ, In his time they were still questioning people when they bring information For example, there was a grandmother or an old woman who came to Abu Bakr AsSiddiq and she said: \"Do I have anything from inheritance?\".", "So Abu Bakr told her: \"I dont see any verse in the Quran, and I do not know any Hadith of the Prophetﷺ that you have anything to take from the inheritance\" Then he asked the people around him, so here it shows that Abu Bakr AsSiddiq is looking for who heard Hadith from the Prophetﷺ Then one of the Companions –AlMughira– he stood up and he said: \"I heard the Prophetﷺ say that she should be given sixth of the inheritance!\" So then Abu Bakr AsSiddiq did not just accept his information –even though he's a reliable person with a strong memory– He even asked him: \"Was there anyone else other than you who heard this information?\"", "Then another Companion, Muhammad Ibn Maslama, he also said \"I heard this information\". So Abu Bakr accepted the information So this idea of scrutiny was there from the beginning, and that's the whole reason we have gradings That is the whole reason we have an Authentic Hadith and a Weak Hadith Because the scholars spent years of grading and looking at those people who are passing down the Hadith, Is this person actually reliable or not? or is he trustworthy or not? And based on all of these years that they spent investigating, They ended up coming to the conclusion whether this is a reliable Hadith or not a reliable Hadith, And that's why Abdullah Ibn AlMubarak, who was from the Salaf, was from the righteous predecessors, Be said that the Chain of Narration –the Isnad– is a part of the religion, And if it wasn't for that Chain of Narration and authentication; anyone will say anything", "And that is the difference between the Islamic Nation and other nations; that they accept unreliable information from anyone Like Bible for example written by unknown people, while Muslims will have to have the biography of every individual in the Chain Someone might ask where are these biographies of these individuals? Where are they coming from? Where are they written? These biographies of these individuals are written in multiple, multitude of different books of Hadith I تهذيبُ التهذيب (Tahdheeb atTahdheeb), تاريخ البخاري (Tareekh AlBukhari) for example, الضعفاء لابن علي (AdDo'afa by Ibn 'Ali) I can name tens of books right now, actually hundreds of books Books that are just relying on having the biographies of the individuals who make those Narrations And these books will have the statements of the people who are contemporary to them So people who are contemporary to the Narrator will either say he was a trustworthy person or they would say he was a weak person", "So these books have their biography, have their life, And have the statements of what their community –who was contemporary to them– said about them It is STRICT to that level! Anyone that we do not know in the Chain of Narration; we will reject that Narration COMPLETELY Because we do not have history about the individual, his reliability, and we do not know what his community said about him Every Chain and any Narration that someone will say to you this is the Authentic Narration, The individuals in the Chain, we are able to show you without a shadow of a doubt, that those people are reliable and trustworthy And we show you their biographies, and I will give an example in a minute But the last thing I want to say, 2 points I want to make..", "One point is that Bukhari for example or certain books of Hadith, The Narrations that are written in these books, it's not only Bukhari who has written those Narrations, You will find other people with other books of Hadith from different regions, from different countries, in a different time, Narrating the same exact information through a different route, through a different source Which shows why we have something called متواتر (Mutawatir) which you have a mass transmission of the same information By individuals who cannot have met each other and took this information from one another, But they were further apart from each other, there were many, multitude of different people That they could not have met each other and agreed that we will narrate this information So the Ahadith in Bukhari, almost every Hadith in Bukhari you will find it narrated in another book, You will find it narrated in the Musnad of Imam Ahmad, Musnad of Ibn Abi Shayba, you'll find it narrated by other Scholars,", "By other individuals, other than Bukhari that narrate the same information through a different route, Which shows that there is multitude of people that heard from the same source and that this source is reliable Even though I mention all of this to you, this is all to do with the Oral Preservation of it But we also have early written Manuscripts of Hadith. So there is no doubt that there is a historicity to the Hadith For example, Hammam Ibn Munabbih who was born in 19AH, 9 years after the death of the Prophetﷺ, He was the student of direct Companion of the Prophet Abu Hurayra He wrote from Abu Hurayra Narrations that he heard directly from the Prophetﷺ and his Sahifa –Sahifat Hammam Ibn Munabbih– We still have it today, found today, carbon dated and you can read it and you can find the Hadiths are there You can read it one by one.", "Anas Ibn Malik he was born in the 1st century, 83 years after the death of the Prophetﷺ, We have his full book. He has a book called مُوَطّأ (Mowatta' Ibn Malik), we have it full today, You can open it today, you can buy it, purchase it, we have its manuscripts So we have very early manuscripts. We have obviously Bukhari and Muslim and.. Tirmidhi, we have many books! We have very early sources as well which have Narrations of the Prophetﷺ Which shows, without a shadow of a doubt, that these Ahadith are historically reliable and they are tracing down to the Prophetﷺ Because these Ahadith that you see carbon dated, you find the other books have the same Ahadith through different roots Which shows that they're all taken from reliable sources even though that this is one manuscript that has a Hadith, You'll find another person who is not Hammam Ibn Munabbih, who is not Abu Hurayra, who has the same exact information,", "Who is from a complete, different country narrating the same exact information that you find in that carbon dated manuscript Which shows WITHOUT A SHADOW OF A DOUBT that it is historically reliable The last thing I want to do is this; is I want to give an example of a Narration, Very basic example to bring the idea closer to the people's mind so let's get a Hadith, a very basic Hadith This Hadith for example here is narrated in Sahih Muslim; Hadith number:650 حَدَّثَنَا يَحْيَى بْنُ يَحْيَى So Yahya Ibn Yahya narrated that Malik heard from Nafi’, who heard from Ibn 'Umar, who heard from the Prophetﷺ So now we have what we called in the beginning: a Chain of Narration, a group of people who are passing down the information, We have Yahya Ibn Yahya, we have Malik, we have Nafi’, we have Ibn 'Umar and then the Prophetﷺ the source of the information", "We said in order for us to accept this information, those individuals have to live close to each other, To have met each other, and have to have gotten information from one another And I also mentioned that we have their biographies and what they did in their life and I will give an example And the example is here in front of us today; Yahya Ibn Yahya, who is Yahya Ibn Yahya? We open one of the books of Ahadith that has the history and biography of the people For example سِيَر أعلام النبلاء (Siyar a’lam anNubala) whose written by an individual called Addhahabi, He tells us now who is this individual who's narrating: Yahya Ibn Yahya?", "He starts first by telling you his name. His name is Ibn Bakr Ibn Abdurrahman, And then he says he’s Shaykh-al-Islam, he gives him a title he says the عالِم خُرَسان. So, he was a Scholar in the region of Khorasan And then he gives you his lineage: Abu Zakaria Attamimi AlMunkari AlNaysaburi AlHafidh. Then he says that he: كَتب ببَلدِه و بالحجاز والعراق والشام ومصر (He wrote Narrations and he wrote information in his country –which is Khorasan– and he did in Hijaz and Iraq and As-Sham and in Egypt) Then it says لَقِيَ صِغاراً مِن التابعين (he met young students of the Companions) For example, he met Kathir Ibn Saleem, he met Abdullah Ibn Ja’far, he met Yazeed Ibn AlMiqdam, he met Zuhayr Ibn Mu'awiya, He met Malik –which we just said he narrated from–, he met Shurayh AlQadi, he met Sa'air, he met Ibn Aqeel, he met Sulayman Ibn Bilal,", "He met Allayth Ibn Sa’d, he met Abdurrahman Ibn Abi AlMawali, he met Attaf, he gives you the people of.. The students of the Companions examples, and he mentions names upon names that he have met And then he also mentions the names of the people who narrated from him, who heard information from him We said Muslim.. is narrating the Narrator he heard from him, AlBukhari heard from him, Muhammad Moosa Ibn AlMarwazi, Heard from him, Ahmed Ibn Sayyar heard from him, 'Uthman Ibn Sa’eed adDarimi heard from him, Muhammad Ibn Yahya adDhuhli Heard from him, his son Yahya narrated and heard from him, Zakariya Ibn Dawood heard from him..", "And then he goes on to what is his date of birth, he was born 142AH –the Islamic Calendar– And then he says what people said about him He said Imam Ahmed Ibn Hanbal –who was a great Scholar- what did he say about him? He said he did not see any one of the people similar to the greatness of Yahya Ibn Yahya. So, he praised him Another individual, Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim, he said Yahya Ibn Yahya died and he was the Scholar of the whole Earth So he's praising him, he's saying he was a reliable individual. And now he goes on..", "There's a long page here of the individuals who spoke about him, who said his reliability, Who said when he was born, who said.. and I can do that with every single person in the Chain The second person in the Chain, alImam Malik. Who is Alimam Malik? His full name and inheritage, he's 'Abdullah Ibn Malik Ibn Anas Ibn Malik Ibn Amir Ibn Hanbal Ibn Hatim Ibn.. I can give all his biography. Which year he was born? He was born 93AH Who did he narrate from? His mother, she was called 'Aliya Bent Shareek. He narrated from azZuhri And he narrated from Sa'eed and Amir Ibn azZubayr Ibn alKindary..", "The point is every single individual in the Chain, same thing! Nafi', who is Nafi'? Nafi' was a student of 'Abdullah Ibn 'Umar What was his name? He was a Scholar, his name was Abu 'Abdillah alQurashi, he was the student of 'Abdullah Ibn 'Umar And now who is 'Abdullah Ibn 'Umar? 'Abdullah Ibn 'Umar was a direct Companion of the Prophetﷺ And he was the son of 'Umar Ibn alKhattab who was the Caliphate of Islam.. Like I can go on and on and give you the whole, full history and biography of every single individual that you see in the Chain in front of you So when we accept any information and we say as Muslims that the Prophet Muhammadﷺ said this, We know for a fact that Prophet Muhammadﷺ said this, because we have the huge..", "The biggest amount of scrutiny towards our Islamic text, because we know as we said that this is RELIGION! And the people took it very seriously that whatever the Prophetﷺ says is very important It is to be passed down to the next Generation, in order for those people to know what to do with their Afterlife So there is NO DOUBT that the Hadith is historically reliable",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali\"")
