#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("OK, so now he's talking about what? People who are from amongst this أمّة (Ummah: Nation) and then when it comes to the Ummah.. You have two types of the Ummah, the people who.. The Ummah of استجابة (Istijabah: Acceptance) and Ummah of the دعوة (Da'wah: Invitation) Ummah can be everyone literally that the Prophetﷺ calls to Islam, the Muslim and the non-Muslim But the Ummah of the Prophetﷺ means the people he was sent to, since his message started And then you have the Ummah of Ijabah, the people who accepted the message, so this Hadith just says Ummah And then it says these people do a lot of righteous deeds, good deeds, like the mountains, good righteous deeds like the mountains.", "But Allahﷻ He causes all of these good deeds to disappear on the Day of Judgment.. Why? why is mentioned in the Hadith. The reason is that they do specific sins in secret. Whenever إِذَا خَلَوْا بِمَحَارِمِ اللَّهِ whenever they are alone, secluded بِمَحَارِمِ اللَّهِ انْتَهَكُوهَا This is the best translation now, every time they are in seclusion or hidden in a hidden specific place that no one is around them They are with Allahﷻ as the only One Who sees them, they break the commands of Allahﷻ So اذا خلوا that means every time, this is a better translation of the Hadith There's a few issues now, the first thing is that this Hadith first is disagreed upon its authenticity The Hadith is the disagreed upon its authenticity, and there is a person in the Chain of Narration He's an individual that there is a disagreement when it comes to his strength in narration", "So, there is a disagreement when it comes to the authenticity of this specific narration, that's the first thing now.. But let's say.. assuming we take the authenticity of the narration and we take the people who authenticated this narration Now there's very problematic things to take.. first, if you are alone you do the sin in secret.. The default position in Islam is that you're supposed to be doing the sins in secret.. You're not supposed to be publicly doing them and sharing them with the people Why? Because the Prophetﷺ said كُلُّ أُمَّتي مُعافًى إلَّا المُجاهِرِينَ every person of my Nation, he would be pardoned except those who..", "ِِِExpose and do their sins out there publicly for other people to see Because when you do it publicly then people see and then the sin does not become.. it becomes normalized And then other people are doing it and then it becomes easier for people to do So it's a lot more egregious for someone to be committing sins publicly So it is absolutely better from an Islamic point of view that you keep the sins that you do between you and Allahﷻ So,... do not listen to this narration and then get a misunderstanding for it, because this is not the case In fact, there is in the Tafsir (exegesis) of the verse of the Quran (Alinshiqaq84:8)..", "فَسَوْفَ يُحاسَبُ حِسابًا يَسِيرًا (that he will be having an easy Hisab (Judgement)) When Allahﷻ holds him accountable in the day of judgment for his deeds.. There is a Hadith which is explaining that the person who hid the sins that he did.. So then Allahﷻ says that you hid them and kept them in secret, so today I'll forgive them no one else knows about them.. You kept them hidden and secret and then Allahﷻ forgives them for not exposing them, so as a Muslim you shouldn't be exposing them But in the same time you shouldn't be thinking that it's OK now when you're alone, you do things and you don't fear Allahﷻ You should always keep in mind that Allahﷻ is watching Because Allahﷻ says in the Quran about the hypocrites the \"منافقون\" which we're going to highlight in a second now (Annisa4:108) يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَا يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ (They hide from the people they don't hide from Allahﷻ", "وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ إِذْ يُبَيِّتُونَ (and he's with them when they're at the night) So, you have to be as a Muslim in the same time while you are hiding the shortcomings that you have.. You shouldn't be thinking that it's OK it's normal now only Allahﷻ sees me so i'm gonna do it You should always have in mind that Allah sees you and that should prevent you as much as possible from committing certain things, Committing certain sins and certain bad acts But this narration here is to be understood to be talking about the hypocrites Yes, the hypocrites were among the Companions, they used to pray and they used to do all of these different things But those are the people that Allahﷻ causes their deeds to go to waste, Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Alfurqan25:23) وَقَدِمْنَآ إِلَىٰ مَا عَمِلُوا۟ مِنْ عَمَلٍۢ فَجَعَلْنَـٰهُ هَبَآءًۭ مَّنثُورًا We came to the deeds they do and then we made them disappear", "So this is referring to disbelievers, so this Hadith here is referring to the Munafiqeen, the Hypocrites, those who were doing major Nifaq (Hypocricy). They were among the Companions. Yeah, they were around them, claiming to be their brothers, they were praying and doing everything But every time إِذَا خَلَوْا that means, every time they go and they are in secret, they mock the religion, they mock Allahﷻ Like Allahﷻ says in Surat (Albqara2:14), He says: وَإِذَا لَقُوا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ قَالُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا (If they see the believers, they say we believe) And then if they وَإِذَا خَلَوْا۟ إِلَىٰ شَيَـٰطِينِهِمْ if they go now to their shayateen (Devils), their other disbelievers, they mock..", "They say, we are actually with you shayateen, we are only mocking the believers So this Hadith is to be understood about, if it's authentic, if you're going to take its authenticity Then as a Muslim, you should understand this Hadith is referring to the Munafiqoon; the people who are hypocrites, major Nifaq Who show belief and then hide disbelief in their hearts But the Muslims, their deeds are not just gone to waste fully like this Because as a Muslim, you're supposed to hide the shortcomings that you have This is the default position, this is what you're supposed to do",))
