#host("Farid Responds", ("Moving on to Hadith number three. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said there is none amongst the Muslims who plants a tree or sows seeds and then a bird or a person or an animal eats from it, but it is regarded as a charitable gift for him. And by charitable gift here, it means that it counts for him as a reward. Anas ibn Malik used to pass by a group of boys and he'd greet them and said, \"The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to do so.\" So, someone may be asking, \"Okay, what's the point of this?", "So what? He's greeting children. What What is this? How's this beneficial?\" Well, guys, this tells you something about the nature of the Prophet, peace be upon him. Like some people, especially disbelievers, they imagine that the Prophet, peace be upon him, was someone that was stern and harsh and and cold. When reality, he was friendly with everyone. He was friendly with children. And I mean, the Hadith in itself is proof of that. Moving on to Hadith number five. Anas narrated that the hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, used to hang down up to his shoulders.", "Now, there are multiple narrations that speak about the length of the hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and it's quite natural that some of them would display the Prophet's hair, peace be upon him, as being longer or shorter. Um however, from what I recall, this is the uh narration with the longest reported hair for the Prophet, peace be upon him. And moving on to Hadith number six. The Prophet said, \"Allah will say to that person off the hellfire who will receive the least punishment, if you had everything on the earth, would you give it as a ransom to free yourself?\"", "He will say, \"Yes.\" Then Allah will say, \"While you were in the backbone of Adam, I asked you much less than this, i.e. not to worship others besides me, but you insisted on worshipping others besides me. On to Hadith number seven. Anas reported Allah's messenger peace be upon him saying, \"The son of Adam grows old, but two desires in him remain young, desire for wealth and desire for life.\" On to Hadith number eight. Narrated Anas that the prophet peace be upon him said, \"None of you will have faith till he wishes for his Muslim brother what he likes for himself.\"", "And on to Hadith number nine. Asim narrated, \"I said to Anas, 'Did Allah's apostle make Medina a sanctuary?'\" He replied, \"Yes, Medina is a sanctuary from such and such place to such and such place. It is forbidden to cut its trees and whoever innovates a heresy in it or commits a sin therein will incur the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.\" Of course, this is referring to the sanctuary of Medina. However, it does also apply to the sanctuary of Mecca. So, feel free to share this report to shirk apologists that would like to see missiles being hurled into Mecca.",))
#source("Source: Farid Responds, \"Test your Knowledge - Ten Hadiths\"")
