#host("Farid Responds", ("So, sometimes you find that like Hadith rejectors or ex-Muslims they say things like I left Islam when I read the Quran or I left the Hadith, I rejected the Hadith after I read the Hadith. you telling me that Hadith rejectors actually sat down and read the Hadith like properly? Like an actual book of Hadith? La. La la la la. And the reason is because the vast majority of the Hadith are not problematic. In fact, a very large number of them have like these indirect Iman boosting type of information. And a lot of it's just like mundane, a lot of mundane information, slice of life information that just makes you appreciate their times.", "And here's something that you may have not come across. It's something I noticed by like piecing narrations together and here's something that I found. You can actually find this in Bukhari and Muslim. Yes, okay. Bukhari and Muslim in which the prophet, peace be upon him, starts speaking about or starts listing the clans of the Ansar and he says that the best of the Ansar are Banu Najjar and then Banu Abdul Ashhal and then Banu Harith bin Khazraj and then Banu Sa'idah. Okay? The narrator of the Hadith is Abu Usaid Sa'idi. He's from Banu Sa'idah. So, he mentions his clan, his subtribe, as like fourth place, right?", "Out of out of the top four clans of the Ansar. And Abu Usaid as-Sa'idi says, \"You're going to accuse me? You going to You You guys are going to accuse me? If I was someone that was going to lie about the prophet, peace be upon him, then I wouldn't mention us as number four.\" By the way, let me just break this down for you guys. Banu Najjar that includes Anas ibn Malik, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Zayd ibn Thabit. It's one of the bigger, well-known clans of the Ansar. Banu Abd al-Ashhal, that's the tribe of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh.", "It's also the tribe of Usayd ibn Hudayr, as well as of course his father, the famous Hudayr al-Kata'ib. And then you have Banu Sa'idah, of course, which is the famous tribe that is known for Saqifah Bani Sa'idah, which is led by Sa'd ibn Ubadah, of course, and in this report, Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi. Now, what I find really interesting here is that Sa'd ibn Ubadah is actually very upset that his clan is mentioned as the fourth. So, what he did was he wanted to, at least, he wanted to prepare. He said he said, \"Prepare my donkey so that I could go to the prophet, peace be upon him.\"", "And basically to speak to him about this. Like it's something that weighed down massively on him. And then he was spoken out of it. And basically he just gave up on the idea of speaking to the prophet, peace be upon him, on his ordering and favoring of the different clans of the Ansar.",))
